$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Outlook it expresses"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"neutral-to-bullish"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Opens with"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"a credit"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Best case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"The premium received"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Worst case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Strike minus premium, if the underlying goes to zero"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Breakeven"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Strike minus premium received"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Exposures"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"delta positive · gamma negative · theta positive · vega negative"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-card border px-[18px] py-4 transition-colors duration-panel ease-standard bg-card border-border shadow-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-3 flex items-center gap-2","children":["$undefined",["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold leading-tight","children":["Lesson",false]}],false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted [&_h1]:mb-2 [&_h1]:text-base [&_h1]:font-bold [&_h1]:text-text [&_h2]:mb-1.5 [&_h2]:mt-5 [&_h2]:text-[13px] [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:text-text [&_h3]:mb-1 [&_h3]:mt-4 [&_h3]:text-[12px] [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:text-text [&_p]:mb-2.5 [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-text [&_ul]:mb-2.5 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ol]:mb-2.5 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-5 [&_li]:mb-1 [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-bg [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:py-0.5 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[11px] [&_code]:text-text [&_table]:mb-3 [&_table]:w-full [&_table]:text-left [&_table]:text-[11.5px] [&_th]:border-b [&_th]:border-border [&_th]:pb-1 [&_th]:pr-3 [&_th]:font-semibold [&_th]:text-text [&_td]:border-b [&_td]:border-border [&_td]:py-1 [&_td]:pr-3 [&_td]:align-top [&_a]:text-teal hover:[&_a]:underline [&_blockquote]:border-l-2 [&_blockquote]:border-border2 [&_blockquote]:pl-3 [&_blockquote]:italic","children":[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Short Put"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":"A short put is one sold put. Premium is received in exchange for the obligation\r\nto take delivery of the underlying at the strike if assigned."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"children":"The structure"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":"One leg: a short put, typically out of the money, in the near expiry. Margin is\r\nblocked at entry."}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":"Maximum loss is large but finite — the underlying cannot fall below zero, so\r\nthe worst case is the strike less the premium received. In an index this bound\r\nis theoretical; in a single stock it is not."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"children":"What it is exposed to"}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Delta"}]," positive — the position gains as the underlying rises."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Gamma"}]," negative. Delta worsens as the underlying falls, so losses accelerate\r\nrather than accrue linearly. As with any short option, gamma magnitude rises\r\nsharply into expiry."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-5",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Theta"}]," positive. Decay accrues to the writer."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-6",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Vega"}]," negative, and this interacts badly with the position's direction.\r\nFalling markets typically raise implied volatility. A short put therefore\r\ntends to lose on delta and vega simultaneously — the loss arrives faster than\r\nthe underlying move alone accounts for. This correlation is what makes short\r\nputs behave worse in a drawdown than their payoff diagram suggests."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"children":"Payoff"}],"\n",["$","p","p-7",{"children":"At or above the strike at expiry, the put expires worthless and the premium is\r\nkept. Below the strike, loss accrues as the underlying falls, offset by the\r\npremium. Breakeven is strike minus premium received."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-3",{"children":"The cash-secured variant"}],"\n",["$","p","p-8",{"children":["If the full strike value is set aside in cash, the structure is a cash-secured\r\nput and the economics change character. Assignment then results in acquiring\r\nthe underlying at the strike, with the premium reducing the effective cost. The\r\nrisk is unchanged in magnitude — it is the same payoff — but it is funded\r\nrather than levered, and no margin call can force an exit at an unfavourable\r\nmoment. See ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/directional/cash-secured-put.md"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-9",{"children":"The distinction matters more in India than the payoff diagram implies, because\r\nthe margin variant and the cash-secured variant have identical diagrams and\r\nentirely different failure modes."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-4",{"children":"Indian market specifics"}],"\n",["$","p","p-10",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Skew works against the seller's entry price and for their carry."}]," Index puts\r\ntrade at higher implied volatility than equidistant calls, so a short put\r\ncollects more premium than a short call at the same distance. That extra\r\npremium is compensation for a real asymmetry, not an inefficiency — downside\r\nmoves in equity indices are faster and larger than upside ones."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-11",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Margin."}]," SPAN plus exposure, marked through the day, with intraday\r\nposition-limit monitoring since April 2025. The 2% expiry-day extreme loss\r\nmargin on short options applies here too."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-12",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Physical settlement."}]," A short stock put finishing in the money obliges\r\n",["$","em","em-0",{"children":"taking"}]," delivery — the full contract value in cash must be available on E+2.\r\nA position sized against margin rather than against contract value can be\r\nseveral times larger than the account can actually settle. Delivery margins\r\nbegin accruing four trading days before expiry, which is the mechanism that\r\nsurfaces the problem before settlement rather than at it."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-13",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Cost."}]," STT of 0.15% of premium on the sale."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-5",{"children":"How it typically fails"}],"\n",["$","p","p-14",{"children":"Selling puts is profitable in most months, which is precisely the difficulty:\r\nthe strategy's own track record encourages size. The loss arrives in the\r\nminority of periods when the underlying falls quickly, and it arrives amplified\r\nby negative gamma, rising implied volatility and, in single stocks, a physical\r\nsettlement obligation sized to contract value rather than to margin."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-6",{"children":"Related"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/vertical-spreads/bull-put-spread.md"}]," — the same leg with a lower\r\nput bought against it, capping the loss at the spread width"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/directional/cash-secured-put.md"}]," — the funded variant"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"risk/tail-risk.md"}]," — why win rate does not describe this payoff"]}],"\n"]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[10px] leading-relaxed text-faint","children":["Educational material describing how a structure behaves. Not a recommendation, not a signal, and not personalised advice. Source: ",["$","code",null,{"className":"font-mono","children":"docs/learning/strategies/directional/short-put.md"}]]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children","$4","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[[null,["$","$L6",null,{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":[["$","title",null,{"children":"404: This page could not be found."}],["$","div",null,{"style":{"fontFamily":"system-ui,